// === PREAMBLE ===
// @trope    Villainous Breakdown
// @category Villains / Psychological
// @source   https://allthetropes.org/wiki/Villainous_Breakdown
// @domain   Narrative
// @version  1.3
//
// Laconic (per the wiki): the moment a villain, watching their carefully laid schemes collapse,
// loses all composure — the suave, in-control mask cracks into screaming rage, gibbering panic,
// or outright madness. The calmer and more collected the villain was, the more spectacular the
// shattering. FRONTIER: names the EMOTION_DYNAMICS appraisal of a schemer's own [&Fails] — the
// inverse of MAGNIFICENT_BASTARD's serene mask. Where the Magnificent Bastard's poise is the
// SOURCE of our regard, the Breakdown is what happens when that poise has nothing left to stand
// on: [#Certain] inverts to [-Certain] [#Afraid], and the composed surface goes [+Volatile]. A
// near-miss of the DESPAIR EVENT HORIZON — the panic of a will that has not yet abandoned hope,
// only its self-command.


// === IMPORTS & ASSOCIATIONS ===
import "trl/modules/emotion_dynamics.trl"   // appraisal of failure -> loss of composure; [#Afraid], fear
import "trl/tropes/the_gambit.trl"          // the plan whose [&Fails] springs the breakdown

// Lateral thematic links (optional, machine-followable — for discovery / embeddings).
assoc villainous_breakdown -> [
  the_gambit            : "the breakdown is the failure mode of",
  magnificent_bastard   : "the cracking of the serene mask of",
  despair_event_horizon : "the panicked near-miss of",
  fear                  : "the composed schemer is overtaken by",
  failure               : "appraises the schemer's own as identity-shattering"
]


// === ONTOLOGY ===
// The composed-villain-unmasked: cunning antagonism whose poise was load-bearing, and shatters
// when the scheme does. (Antagonist a prelude role, Cunning/Volatile prelude props — reused.)

imply VillainousBreakdown -> [Antagonist, Cunning, Volatile, Narrative]


// === ABSTRACT RULE ===
// Recognition: a composed [+Antagonist] [+Cunning] [#Certain] villain — certainty being the
// outward sign of the in-control mask — suffers the failure of their own scheme ([&Fails], the
// failure mode of The Gambit). The appraisal of that failure cracks the mask: certainty inverts
// ([-Certain]), the surface goes [+Volatile], and the dread the poise was holding back surfaces
// as [#Afraid]. The schemer becomes [+VillainousBreakdown]. (The composure must be present FIRST
// — [#Certain] in the when: — so the rule fires on the COLLAPSE of control, not on a villain who
// was panicky all along. It stops short of the Despair Event Horizon: a will undone, not abandoned.)
rule VillainousBreakdown {
  when:
    char $villain [+Antagonist] [+Cunning] [#Certain]
    evt  $collapse [&Fails(agent=$villain)]
  then:
    $villain [-Certain]
    $villain [+Volatile]
    $villain [#Afraid(source=$collapse)]
    $villain [+VillainousBreakdown]
    $villain -- fear
}


// === CONCRETE VIGNETTE: One Flew Over the Cuckoo's Nest — Nurse Ratched, the ward erupts (film, 1975) ===
// Nurse Ratched runs Ward 3 as a glacial machine of routine and quiet humiliation — never raising
// her voice, her control so total it reads as serenity. Her scheme is the ward itself: the men
// kept docile, McMurphy's rebellion contained by procedure. When the ward erupts — the party, the
// broken window, Billy Bibbit's suicide laid at her feet and McMurphy's hands at her throat — the
// machine of her composure fails. The flat administrative calm finally cracks: the certainty that
// the system would hold is gone, the voice rises, the unflappable mask shows fear. The institution
// reasserts itself, but the woman who never lost control has, for once and visibly, lost it.

// NURSE RATCHED — the glacial-calm administrator; control IS the scheme
char ratched [+Antagonist] [+Cunning] [#Certain]

// RANDLE McMURPHY — the rebellion that breaks the routine
char mcmurphy [+Protagonist]

// INT. WARD 3, STATE MENTAL HOSPITAL - DAY
set ward [+Interior] [+Day]
ward [+Institutional]

scene the_mask_cracks {
  beat 1 {
    ratched @ ward
    mcmurphy @ ward
    // The control holds: the ward runs on her routine, the men managed by procedure.
    ratched -- mcmurphy : "Contains"
  }
  beat 2 {
    // The ward erupts — Billy's death, McMurphy's hands at her throat. Her scheme of control fails.
    evt the_eruption [&Fails(agent=ratched)]
        dialog(inject=[speaker=ratched], inline="""
               speaker: "{speaker}"
               cue: "the flat administrative calm gone, the voice finally rising, fear on the unflappable face"
               tone: cracked, no longer serene
               text: "The best thing we can do is go on with our daily routine."
               """)
    ratched [-Certain]
    ratched [+Volatile]
    ratched [#Afraid(source=the_eruption)]
    ratched [+VillainousBreakdown]
    ratched -- fear
    // VillainousBreakdown — the composed mask ([#Certain]) shatters into [-Certain] [+Volatile] [#Afraid]
  }
}
